===== checks/runs-artifacts.py:443-462  fn=_tracked_tops  verbs=['ls-tree'] shape=LINEWISE keyed_container=True
    443| def _tracked_tops(root=ROOT):
    444|     """EVERY directory prefix of every file `git ls-tree -r HEAD` names, at EVERY depth.
    445| 
    446|     **MY OWN MEASUREMENT WAS WRONG HERE AND THE BEFORE-VALUE WAS A CLEAN, CONFIDENT WRONG ANSWER.**
    447|     The first version recorded a top-level directory as tracked only if a tracked file sat AT its
    448|     root, which is true of `checks/` and false of `.agents/` -- so it printed `tracked=0` for a
    449|     directory holding **4,496** tracked files, and `.agents/` came out of `unrecoverable_dirs()` as
    450|     a deletion target. `runs/` is genuinely absent from the tree, and one level of prefix was
    451|     enough to tell those apart by accident. A depth-1 lookup is a basename shape.
    452| 
    453|     **NOT `git ls-files`**: MEASURED 2026-10-06, `jj git colocation` stages an empty blob for every
    454|     untracked file, so the index carries 906 `--intent-to-add` placeholders and reading it answers a
    455|     question about the editor, not about the repository.
    456|     """
    457|     pref: set[str] = set()
