===== checks/slop-declare.py:136-151  fn=tracked  verbs=['ls-files', 'ls-tree'] shape=LINEWISE keyed_container=False
    136| def tracked(root: Path) -> list[str] | None:
    137|     """Every path in the TREE, or None if git did not answer. `-z`, so a space in a name is data.
    138| 
    139|     **`git ls-tree -r HEAD`, NOT `git ls-files`** — and this is the **third** population in this tree read
    140|     from the INDEX. `declaretwo` MEASURED WHY IT MATTERS HERE: **THE INDEX CARRIED 282 DIRECTORIES AT
    141|     18:45 AND 460 AT 19:31 — IT MOVED BY 178 IN 46 MINUTES WITH NO COMMIT** — and the SAME INSTRUMENT
    142|     over three revisions reads **250 -> 262 -> 265**. **`orcdecide`'s 256 AND `declare`'s 262 WERE NOT
    143|     MISCOUNTS; THEY READ `git ls-files`, WHICH IS AN INDEX THIS TREE HAS RESET SIX TIMES TONIGHT.**
    144|     ***A POPULATION READ FROM A THING BEING REBUILT UNDER IT IS NOT A POPULATION, IT IS A READING OF
    145|     THE WEATHER.** The REVISION IS PRINTED ON EVERY RUN (`rev()`), because a count without the commit it
    146|     was measured at is `pinindep`'s finding with a different subject.
    147|     """
    148|     p = git(root, "ls-tree", "-r", "-z", "--name-only", "HEAD")
    149|     if p.returncode != 0:
    150|         return None
    151|     return [f for f in p.stdout.split("\0") if f]

===== checks/sweep.py:842-859  fn=tracked_files  verbs=['ls-files'] shape=LINEWISE keyed_container=False
    842| def tracked_files(root: str = ROOT) -> set[str]:
    843|     """`git ls-files` MINUS the tracked-but-deleted.
    844| 
    845|     `git ls-files` RETURNS TRACKED-BUT-DELETED PATHS, so membership tested against it alone calls a
    846|     file committed when it is not on disk at all -- and an uncommitted row would then be deleted as
    847|     if `git` could restore it.
    848| 
    849|     **`os.path.lexists`, NOT `Path.exists()`: `exists()` FOLLOWS SYMLINKS AND THIS TREE HAS 167 OF
    850|     THEM**, so a dangling link inside `.slop` is reported here as ABSENT while `git` tracks it, and a
    851|     tracked row would be called untracked on the strength of a link's target.
    852| 
    853|     MEASURED, because the count was quoted as a defect that has since stopped being one: `git
    854|     ls-files` returns 4,609 paths on this tree and **all 4,609 are on disk -- 0 phantom, 0 entries
    855|     carrying the intent-to-add empty-blob SHA `e69de29`.** The 4,109 figure in circulation was true
    856|     earlier today and is FALSE NOW, which is exactly why a premise that is not re-measured decays.
    857|     """
    858|     r = subprocess.run(["git", "ls-files", "-z"], cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True)
    859|     return {p for p in r.stdout.split("\0") if p and os.path.lexists(os.path.join(root, p))}

