    279| def commit_view(root, sha):
    280|     """(present, deleted, removed, changed) for one commit.
    281| 
    282|     `deleted` is the `D` set under rename detection (`-M`), so a pure MOVE is not a delete --
    283|     and it is the set the MESSAGE lane judges against, UNCHANGED.
    284| 
    285|     `removed` is `D` PLUS every rename SOURCE, and it is a SEPARATE set for a reason that is a
    286|     measurement rather than a preference: `c83f04ad1c12` reverted 46 renames and git records
    287|     them as `R100`, so `deleted` sees NONE of them -- which is exactly why they were
    288|     "invisible in a diffstat". A rename removes its source path; a set built from `D` alone
    289|     cannot see a removal. Folding the two would CHANGE this lane's verdicts (a claim about a
    290|     rename source would become witnessed), and this lane's verdicts are not this unit's to move.
    291| 
    292|     The two sets are kept apart so ONE commit can carry two subjects -- the DIFF-removal and
    293|     the MESSAGE-claim -- and each has its own verdict. See `gates/README.md`.
    294|     """
